  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "This study presents a deep learning-based approach to automatically quantify turning angles in Parkinson's disease, focusing on continuous, real-world gait analysis. The method uses 3D human mesh recovery and motion embeddings to estimate turning steps in a home setting, achieving accurate results with a high level of precision.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The first study explores the use of single monocular camera data to quantify turning angles in Parkinson's patients in a home setting.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The method achieves a turning calculation accuracy of 41.6% and a weighted precision of 68.3% for Turn-REMAP.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The study includes a 1386 turning video clip dataset from 24 subjects, validated using Turn-H3.6M.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
